1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:00,992
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,017 --> 00:00:02,038
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,063 --> 00:00:03,107
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,132 --> 00:00:03,994
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,019 --> 00:00:04,936
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:05,724 --> 00:00:08,504
Golf may not be a game
for the most skilled.

7
00:00:08,529 --> 00:00:10,984
But it is a game
for those who never give up.

8
00:00:11,009 --> 00:00:13,638
We may miss a shot or
hit the ball out of the fairway,

9
00:00:13,663 --> 00:00:15,798
but we never run from
the obstacles ahead.

10
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:20,365
Life is the same.
No one wins every hole.

11
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:22,663
But the strongest among us

12
00:00:22,688 --> 00:00:25,180
are those who dare to face
their own mistakes

13
00:00:25,205 --> 00:00:27,770
and find a new way to deal
with them without hesitation.

14
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:29,021
Love is the same.

15
00:00:29,046 --> 00:00:30,593
If you're afraid of
making a mistake,

16
00:00:30,618 --> 00:00:32,393
you'll never truly play the game.

17
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,607
We have to dare to take the shot,
dare to take risks.

18
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:36,160
and dare to face
the consequences,

19
00:00:36,185 --> 00:00:38,185
whatever the outcome may be.

20
00:00:38,497 --> 00:00:41,769
Many think
golf is all about distance.

21
00:00:41,794 --> 00:00:44,654
But golf isn't a sport
won by sheer power.

22
00:00:44,679 --> 00:00:47,179
It's about learning to control
your own heart.

23
00:00:47,204 --> 00:00:50,539
Because on the course, no one
is fighting us but ourselves.

24
00:00:50,564 --> 00:00:52,204
Every hole is a question.

25
00:00:52,229 --> 00:00:53,949
Every swing is an answer.

26
00:00:53,996 --> 00:00:56,952
Because a true golfer doesn't win
by hitting the best shots,

27
00:00:56,977 --> 00:00:59,317
but by refusing
to give up on themselves.

28
00:01:02,163 --> 00:01:04,888
(Pro Kaimook - Thidapa Kitjakarn)

29
00:01:10,759 --> 00:01:14,280
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

30
00:01:14,915 --> 00:01:16,576
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

31
00:01:16,608 --> 00:01:20,245
♪ It's plain to see ♪

32
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:22,397
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

33
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:25,759
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

34
00:01:26,532 --> 00:01:28,215
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

35
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:31,805
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

36
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:34,020
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

37
00:01:34,045 --> 00:01:36,922
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

38
00:01:36,947 --> 00:01:38,781
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

39
00:01:38,806 --> 00:01:41,657
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

40
00:01:41,682 --> 00:01:44,511
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

41
00:01:44,536 --> 00:01:48,394
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

42
00:01:48,419 --> 00:01:50,439
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

43
00:01:50,464 --> 00:01:53,305
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

44
00:01:53,330 --> 00:01:56,703
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

45
00:01:56,728 --> 00:02:01,479
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

46
00:02:01,504 --> 00:02:03,554
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

47
00:02:04,904 --> 00:02:07,007
Thank you all so, so much.

48
00:02:07,032 --> 00:02:09,899
None of this would've turned out
this well without all of you.

49
00:02:09,924 --> 00:02:11,440
Allez, allez!

50
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,465
- Allez, allez!
- Allez, allez!

51
00:02:13,490 --> 00:02:16,795
- Allez, allez!
- Allez, allez!

52
00:02:16,827 --> 00:02:19,843
Nana, are you okay?

53
00:02:19,876 --> 00:02:21,555
- Allez, allez!
- Allez, allez!

54
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:23,381
Oh, Miss Nana!

55
00:02:23,406 --> 00:02:25,850
The doctor said you probably
haven't been getting enough rest.

56
00:02:25,875 --> 00:02:27,235
and are just feeling fatigued.

57
00:02:27,918 --> 00:02:30,102
- Oh, Mr. Sanchai.
- Hello, Doctor.

58
00:02:30,417 --> 00:02:32,406
About your chemotherapy
treatment plan...

59
00:02:32,431 --> 00:02:34,726
Have you decided
when you'd like to start?

60
00:02:58,198 --> 00:02:59,357
You're awake?

61
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,587
Is it morning already, Vee?

62
00:03:06,084 --> 00:03:08,540
- About last night...
- Oh!

63
00:03:09,684 --> 00:03:12,027
Let's not talk about last night.

64
00:03:15,983 --> 00:03:19,686
It'd be nice to wake up
next to you every morning, Vee.

65
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:22,310
You'd really want that?

66
00:03:22,834 --> 00:03:24,016
Why not?

67
00:03:27,523 --> 00:03:29,968
We don't have to wake up
next to each other every morning.

68
00:03:29,993 --> 00:03:32,660
Wouldn't it be better
if we had each other every day?

69
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:46,701
What are you doing, Vee?

70
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:49,297
The sun's in my eyes.
It's hurting.

71
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:52,389
I'm going to take a shower.

72
00:03:53,326 --> 00:03:55,612
- I'm not letting you go.
- Vee!

73
00:03:56,523 --> 00:03:59,975
What are you doing, Vee?

74
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:02,460
- Take that!
- That tickles!

75
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:07,778
- I'm hungry.
- What do you want to eat?

76
00:04:07,803 --> 00:04:09,951
- Anything's fine.
- Good morning, Nana. Pro Vee.

77
00:04:09,976 --> 00:04:11,318
- Morning.
- Morning.

78
00:04:11,343 --> 00:04:12,780
Hi, Nana.

79
00:04:13,535 --> 00:04:15,870
Oh, Fahsai.

80
00:04:16,258 --> 00:04:17,768
Good morning, Pro Vee.

81
00:04:18,206 --> 00:04:19,477
What a coincidence.

82
00:04:19,502 --> 00:04:21,502
I just went by the clubhouse,

83
00:04:21,527 --> 00:04:23,251
and they said you might be
at the office.

84
00:04:23,683 --> 00:04:26,310
Oh, do you have a lesson today,
Fahsai?

85
00:04:27,421 --> 00:04:30,064
No, but I'm free today,

86
00:04:30,089 --> 00:04:31,920
so I thought I'd drop by.

87
00:04:31,945 --> 00:04:34,311
But I checked your schedule,

88
00:04:34,336 --> 00:04:36,336
and you're free today.

89
00:04:39,282 --> 00:04:41,675
You're free today, Pro Vee?

90
00:04:44,625 --> 00:04:46,625
Uh...

91
00:04:48,314 --> 00:04:49,763
- I'm not.
- What?

92
00:04:49,788 --> 00:04:53,433
But the staff at the course said
you were free until this evening.

93
00:04:53,863 --> 00:04:55,444
- I'm not.
- Pro Vee...

94
00:04:55,469 --> 00:04:58,516
Pro Vee must have
a meeting about...

95
00:05:00,313 --> 00:05:04,655
Um, choosing a new type of grass
to test on the course.

96
00:05:05,235 --> 00:05:07,050
A meeting
that lasts all afternoon?

97
00:05:07,963 --> 00:05:09,479
Mm-hmm. That's right.

98
00:05:09,614 --> 00:05:12,860
- Just about the grass?
- Mm-hmm.

99
00:05:14,969 --> 00:05:16,393
That's too bad.

100
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:18,816
Are you free tomorrow then?

101
00:05:18,841 --> 00:05:21,064
You probably don't remember
your own schedule.

102
00:05:21,089 --> 00:05:22,978
I'll check the system for you.

103
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,997
Tomorrow... booked.

104
00:05:27,162 --> 00:05:28,793
The day after... booked.

105
00:05:28,968 --> 00:05:32,723
And the days after that...
booked, booked, booked.

106
00:05:33,218 --> 00:05:34,808
Sorry, Fahsai.

107
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:37,643
Pro Vee's schedule
is packed until...

108
00:05:37,668 --> 00:05:38,850
the end of the month.

109
00:05:38,953 --> 00:05:40,369
That busy?

110
00:05:41,274 --> 00:05:42,274
Yep.

111
00:05:43,307 --> 00:05:44,798
If you want to improve
your swing,

112
00:05:44,823 --> 00:05:46,502
I can recommend another pro.

113
00:05:46,526 --> 00:05:48,194
They're just as good. Want me to?

114
00:05:49,258 --> 00:05:52,262
No, I don't want to change pros.

115
00:05:52,533 --> 00:05:54,962
Sorry, Fahsai.

116
00:05:54,987 --> 00:05:57,743
Vee and I have another meeting.
We should go.

117
00:05:57,768 --> 00:05:59,825
Oh, wait, wait, wait!

118
00:05:59,866 --> 00:06:00,897
Here.

119
00:06:01,318 --> 00:06:04,338
I got something for Pro Vee, too.

120
00:06:04,553 --> 00:06:07,770
It's a handcrafted grey sedge
handbag from Phatthalung.

121
00:06:08,009 --> 00:06:09,826
- Thank you.
- Can you take a picture of me?

122
00:06:10,924 --> 00:06:11,965
Sure.

123
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:16,828
One, two, three... Beautiful!

124
00:06:16,868 --> 00:06:19,615
Mm, you look so cute, Pro Vee.
That's a wrap.

125
00:06:23,115 --> 00:06:25,613
We'll get going.
We're gonna be late. Come on.

126
00:06:27,854 --> 00:06:30,372
You're really wicked, Nana.

127
00:06:30,747 --> 00:06:32,860
I can be much worse,

128
00:06:32,885 --> 00:06:34,656
if she weren't my friend.

129
00:06:51,058 --> 00:06:54,335
On behalf of Goodview Golf Club,
I'd like to thank you all

130
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:58,187
for choosing us to host today's
Golf Course Network meeting.

131
00:07:00,245 --> 00:07:02,726
Before we begin the meeting
at 1 PM,

132
00:07:02,751 --> 00:07:06,315
we'd like to welcome you all
with a special lunch.

133
00:07:06,871 --> 00:07:09,272
That's wonderful.
I've heard for a while

134
00:07:09,748 --> 00:07:11,804
that everything here
is delicious.

135
00:07:12,654 --> 00:07:13,683
Isn't that right, Nut?

136
00:07:13,993 --> 00:07:15,000
It is.

137
00:07:15,818 --> 00:07:17,924
And what if
we fall in love with it?

138
00:07:19,701 --> 00:07:22,778
We might have to steal the chef,
or maybe buy the whole course.

139
00:07:25,573 --> 00:07:27,102
I don't think it'll come to that.

140
00:07:27,427 --> 00:07:29,427
Our course offers delivery.

141
00:07:29,619 --> 00:07:32,154
If you can't make it here,
you can always order in.

142
00:07:33,282 --> 00:07:34,467
That's great.

143
00:07:34,492 --> 00:07:36,727
I think my course
needs something like that.

144
00:07:37,241 --> 00:07:38,343
You're more than welcome.

145
00:07:38,368 --> 00:07:39,810
If there's something
that works well,

146
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,561
feel free to adapt it
for your own course.

147
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:42,989
I don't mind sharing.

148
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:44,725
How generous of you.

149
00:07:45,209 --> 00:07:47,209
Yes. If I weren't so generous,

150
00:07:47,234 --> 00:07:52,680
you wouldn't be sitting
right here with us today.

151
00:08:01,486 --> 00:08:03,743
Greetings, esteemed guests!

152
00:08:03,768 --> 00:08:07,078
Chef Queen here.
Your lunch is ready!

153
00:08:07,275 --> 00:08:10,234
Our course offers a wide
variety of international cuisine,

154
00:08:10,259 --> 00:08:13,562
including French cuisine,

155
00:08:18,611 --> 00:08:20,848
and all four regions
of Thai cuisine.

156
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,126
Feel all the feeling.

157
00:08:58,098 --> 00:09:00,389
Please enjoy!

158
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:02,279
- Please, help yourselves.
- Enjoy, everyone.

159
00:09:10,856 --> 00:09:13,151
The main agenda for today is

160
00:09:13,176 --> 00:09:17,089
the All Star
Women's Golf Tournament.

161
00:09:17,477 --> 00:09:20,164
Women's golf is gaining
popularity in our country.

162
00:09:20,189 --> 00:09:23,317
I believe we should seize
this opportunity

163
00:09:23,342 --> 00:09:26,192
to support and promote the sport,

164
00:09:26,217 --> 00:09:28,553
and help make golf
more widespread.

165
00:09:28,578 --> 00:09:30,001
And in the future,

166
00:09:30,026 --> 00:09:34,623
we could also organize events
for children, youth, and seniors.

167
00:09:34,786 --> 00:09:38,452
Each course will send
one representative

168
00:09:38,477 --> 00:09:40,205
to compete in the tournament.

169
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:43,776
And whichever course's player
wins will represent us

170
00:09:43,801 --> 00:09:48,265
in the Asian Tour
taking place later this year.

171
00:09:49,733 --> 00:09:52,166
What course will host
the tournament?

172
00:09:52,191 --> 00:09:54,124
If we're looking for
the biggest course,

173
00:09:54,149 --> 00:09:55,995
wouldn't that be Siam Green Golf?

174
00:09:56,201 --> 00:09:57,480
I'm afraid not.

175
00:09:57,505 --> 00:09:59,977
We're currently undergoing
a major renovation.

176
00:10:00,699 --> 00:10:03,081
The Royal Green is available.
We're ready to host.

177
00:10:04,051 --> 00:10:06,688
But the course
hosting the tournament

178
00:10:06,713 --> 00:10:10,581
also needs to have a hotel or
accommodations for the golfers.

179
00:10:10,606 --> 00:10:11,838
That's true.

180
00:10:11,863 --> 00:10:14,413
Especially for players
coming from other provinces,

181
00:10:14,438 --> 00:10:17,207
and the media coming
to cover the event.

182
00:10:17,661 --> 00:10:19,535
There's a hotel near our course.

183
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,323
It's only a little over
ten kilometers away.

184
00:10:21,348 --> 00:10:23,093
I'd call that pretty far.

185
00:10:25,519 --> 00:10:28,783
In that case,
Goodview could be another option.

186
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,763
Our hotel was just renovated,

187
00:10:32,216 --> 00:10:34,224
and I'm confident
it can accommodate everyone.

188
00:10:34,249 --> 00:10:37,602
And the hotel is less than
a kilometer from the course.

189
00:10:44,083 --> 00:10:45,143
That sounds good.

190
00:10:45,683 --> 00:10:48,971
The course is spacious and
has all the necessary facilities.

191
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:52,794
Then it's settled.

192
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:55,373
I think this would be
the most suitable venue.

193
00:11:09,498 --> 00:11:12,281
I'll work out the details
for the tournament preparations

194
00:11:12,306 --> 00:11:14,523
and present the plan in two days.

195
00:11:15,269 --> 00:11:16,618
Thank you, Nut.

196
00:11:17,445 --> 00:11:20,147
So, Nana, who will you send
to represent our course?

197
00:11:25,129 --> 00:11:28,140
Represent us? What do you mean?

198
00:11:28,608 --> 00:11:31,023
The Golf Course Network
is organizing a tournament...

199
00:11:31,974 --> 00:11:35,122
Ms. Nana, it's bad.
Something big has happened.

200
00:11:37,034 --> 00:11:39,034
The wastewater is this close?

201
00:11:39,344 --> 00:11:41,729
How are we supposed to eat
with this right here?

202
00:11:41,754 --> 00:11:42,777
Where are they?

203
00:11:44,914 --> 00:11:47,707
No one's taking responsibility.
No one's doing anything about it.

204
00:11:47,732 --> 00:11:50,298
- How are you going to fix this?
- The villagers are suffering.

205
00:11:50,323 --> 00:11:52,443
- Everyone, everyone!
- This isn't right.

206
00:11:52,468 --> 00:11:54,062
Please, everyone, calm down.

207
00:11:54,298 --> 00:11:56,273
I think there's been
a misunderstanding.

208
00:11:56,368 --> 00:11:58,866
Misunderstood what? It's right
in front of us, isn't it?

209
00:11:58,891 --> 00:11:59,953
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

210
00:11:59,978 --> 00:12:03,019
The water reeks, and look at all
the dead fish floating around.

211
00:12:03,044 --> 00:12:05,673
It stinks everywhere. How are we
supposed to live like this?

212
00:12:06,888 --> 00:12:09,016
You keep the nice,
clean places for yourselves,

213
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:10,858
and dump
all the filthy stuff on us.

214
00:12:10,883 --> 00:12:13,210
That's selfish, you hear me?

215
00:12:13,235 --> 00:12:14,241
Am I right, everyone?

216
00:12:14,266 --> 00:12:16,934
- That's right! Selfish!
- Selfish!

217
00:12:16,959 --> 00:12:20,890
If this is how it's going to be,
we can't live together anymore.

218
00:12:20,915 --> 00:12:22,577
We won't stand for this. No way!

219
00:12:22,602 --> 00:12:24,299
Right, everyone?

220
00:12:24,324 --> 00:12:26,031
- Let's talk this out.
- Then what are you gonna do?

221
00:12:26,056 --> 00:12:27,896
We can't even eat or drink
properly anymore.

222
00:12:27,921 --> 00:12:29,626
Everyone, please, hear me out.

223
00:12:31,304 --> 00:12:33,276
As the owner of this place,

224
00:12:33,301 --> 00:12:36,111
I'm sorry to hear about
the trouble you're going through.

225
00:12:36,136 --> 00:12:39,074
But could you give me some time
to look into the facts first?

226
00:12:39,272 --> 00:12:41,272
Are you trying to
shirk responsibility?

227
00:12:41,909 --> 00:12:44,287
We've heard people say that
so many times before.

228
00:12:44,312 --> 00:12:45,947
And in the end,
nothing ever happens.

229
00:12:46,130 --> 00:12:47,285
That's not what I'm doing.

230
00:12:47,310 --> 00:12:49,165
Our golf course
has been part of this community

231
00:12:49,189 --> 00:12:51,032
since my grandfather's time.

232
00:12:51,205 --> 00:12:53,890
We've never had anything
like this happen before, have we?

233
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:57,770
If the wastewater is coming
from our course,

234
00:12:57,795 --> 00:12:59,167
I'll take responsibility.

235
00:12:59,562 --> 00:13:01,030
How will you take responsibility?

236
00:13:01,175 --> 00:13:04,339
I'll do whatever it takes
to restore the water source

237
00:13:04,364 --> 00:13:06,823
and improve the environment
for everyone in the community.

238
00:13:07,058 --> 00:13:08,401
But how can we trust you?

239
00:13:08,426 --> 00:13:10,426
Exactly. What do we do, everyone?

240
00:13:10,563 --> 00:13:12,682
- We can't live with that stench!
- It's awful!

241
00:13:12,707 --> 00:13:14,446
- The fish are dead!
- They can't handle it.

242
00:13:14,471 --> 00:13:15,605
Hear her out first.

243
00:13:17,174 --> 00:13:22,111
All right, then. We'll give you
three more days.

244
00:13:22,971 --> 00:13:24,518
Then we'll come back
for an answer.

245
00:13:37,138 --> 00:13:39,876
I'm sure the wastewater
didn't come from our course.

246
00:13:40,193 --> 00:13:43,063
We had the treatment system
inspected just last week.

247
00:13:43,088 --> 00:13:44,357
Everything was fine.

248
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:48,014
The chemicals can't reach
the community water source.

249
00:13:48,498 --> 00:13:50,261
We only have three days.

250
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:52,034
Where should we start?

251
00:13:52,201 --> 00:13:53,946
We need to find evidence

252
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:56,560
to prove our innocence
and win the villagers back.

253
00:13:57,782 --> 00:14:00,119
Should we collect water samples
and have them tested?

254
00:14:00,144 --> 00:14:01,181
Good idea.

255
00:14:01,206 --> 00:14:04,451
That could be the evidence
we need to prove we're innocent.

256
00:14:04,713 --> 00:14:07,369
Miss Nana, there's a problem!

257
00:14:07,837 --> 00:14:10,037
Perfect. You're all here.
Let's figure it out together.

258
00:14:10,062 --> 00:14:14,239
Someone posted that they ordered
delivery from our course,

259
00:14:14,264 --> 00:14:16,369
but the food arrived spoiled.

260
00:14:16,393 --> 00:14:18,640
Here's another one.
This person says

261
00:14:18,665 --> 00:14:21,381
they ordered our food,
then got food poisoning.

262
00:14:21,406 --> 00:14:22,708
This is really bad.

263
00:14:22,732 --> 00:14:24,524
It hurts our rating.
They gave us one star.

264
00:14:24,549 --> 00:14:25,862
And here's another one.

265
00:14:25,887 --> 00:14:28,791
They say they ordered our food,
but never received it,

266
00:14:28,816 --> 00:14:30,732
yet they were still charged
through the app.

267
00:14:30,757 --> 00:14:32,376
But is any of this true,
Chef Queen?

268
00:14:33,598 --> 00:14:35,854
I think someone's
trying to sabotage us.

269
00:14:35,879 --> 00:14:38,029
Why do you think
someone's sabotaging us?

270
00:14:38,521 --> 00:14:42,000
Miss Nana, I've been cooking
for over 20 years.

271
00:14:42,025 --> 00:14:45,184
When it comes to food quality,
I check every dish that goes out.

272
00:14:45,209 --> 00:14:47,669
And as for delivery, I don't
think we could've messed up.

273
00:14:47,694 --> 00:14:50,163
We've practiced it so many times.
No way.

274
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:56,124
Looks like all the posts
came from the same email address.

275
00:14:56,149 --> 00:14:57,357
They just changed the names.

276
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,317
Want a drink?

277
00:15:19,976 --> 00:15:20,991
What?

278
00:15:21,452 --> 00:15:23,238
A student at the course
brought it as a gift.

279
00:15:23,477 --> 00:15:25,057
Plum wine from Phrae.

280
00:15:26,486 --> 00:15:27,487
Want to try it?

281
00:15:27,955 --> 00:15:30,288
Just one glass.
I've still got work to finish.

282
00:15:34,787 --> 00:15:38,445
I heard things got pretty hectic
at the course today.

283
00:15:39,058 --> 00:15:41,927
That's why I'm still
working this late.

284
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:52,587
Why does everything
always end up on your plate?

285
00:15:53,414 --> 00:15:56,339
I guess I'm the most efficient
person at the course.

286
00:15:58,177 --> 00:15:59,471
Proud of yourself?

287
00:15:59,683 --> 00:16:02,754
Of course.
Whenever there was a problem,

288
00:16:03,088 --> 00:16:04,738
Mr. Sanchai would send me in.

289
00:16:05,045 --> 00:16:08,687
Just like now, when I'm Nana's
right-hand woman.

290
00:16:11,165 --> 00:16:14,240
Why doesn't Miss Nana
find another left hand?

291
00:16:14,741 --> 00:16:17,617
Then her right hand
could have some private time.

292
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,740
Can I help you with anything?

293
00:16:26,273 --> 00:16:27,375
I've got a free hand.

294
00:16:28,137 --> 00:16:29,312
I'm fine.

295
00:16:31,951 --> 00:16:35,883
So Jinny's hand right here

296
00:16:36,502 --> 00:16:38,718
can't help
Miss right hand at all?

297
00:17:02,668 --> 00:17:04,129
Is this better?

298
00:17:06,462 --> 00:17:07,774
Thank you.

299
00:17:12,346 --> 00:17:14,678
Starting to see the benefits
of my hand, huh?

300
00:17:21,955 --> 00:17:23,160
What do you want?

301
00:17:24,953 --> 00:17:27,574
Just checking on you.

302
00:17:32,307 --> 00:17:34,167
Don't beat around the bush.

303
00:17:34,192 --> 00:17:36,064
I still have a lot of work
to finish.

304
00:20:57,752 --> 00:21:00,452
But the canal water
really does smell bad, Nut.

305
00:21:00,715 --> 00:21:02,460
Mm. It really does.

306
00:21:02,874 --> 00:21:05,376
But the smell isn't coming
from the water, Nana.

307
00:21:05,401 --> 00:21:06,773
What do you mean?

308
00:21:06,965 --> 00:21:09,222
It's coming
from around the canal.

309
00:21:09,619 --> 00:21:11,678
Then what about
all those dead fish?

310
00:21:11,703 --> 00:21:12,844
There were so many of them.

311
00:21:12,930 --> 00:21:14,824
That almost
made it convincing, too.

312
00:21:14,849 --> 00:21:17,420
But the fish that washed up dead
are marine fish,

313
00:21:17,609 --> 00:21:19,043
not freshwater fish.

314
00:21:19,068 --> 00:21:21,455
So the samples you had Belle send
for testing,

315
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,849
the water and the dead fish...

316
00:21:23,874 --> 00:21:28,566
Exactly. The test results will
prove our course is innocent.

317
00:21:29,811 --> 00:21:33,435
Are you saying our course
is being framed?

318
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:39,657
Then who's behind it?
And why would they do this?

319
00:21:47,842 --> 00:21:49,241
Everyone! Manager!

320
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:51,665
The packaging is definitely
from our course.

321
00:21:51,690 --> 00:21:52,942
It's from my restaurant,

322
00:21:52,967 --> 00:21:55,548
but I didn't
make the food inside.

323
00:21:55,573 --> 00:21:58,685
It's not ours. Look at the basil.

324
00:21:58,710 --> 00:22:00,846
That's not how I cut my squid.

325
00:22:04,402 --> 00:22:07,116
I don't know who messed up,

326
00:22:07,141 --> 00:22:10,428
but it didn't sit right with me,
so I called to check.

327
00:22:10,453 --> 00:22:12,534
I asked whether anyone
had placed an order

328
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:14,443
around the same time
they posted those reviews.

329
00:22:14,468 --> 00:22:17,729
But no one had even ordered
any of those dishes.

330
00:22:18,499 --> 00:22:20,209
Chef Queen,
do you suspect anyone?

331
00:22:22,122 --> 00:22:23,618
Could it be March?

332
00:22:25,455 --> 00:22:27,836
Ms. Yupadee from The Royal Green.

333
00:22:30,128 --> 00:22:32,859
I'm not trying to accuse anyone,

334
00:22:32,884 --> 00:22:35,764
but Pro Jin once told me

335
00:22:35,789 --> 00:22:38,651
she'd seen Pro Vee
at Ms. Yupadee's course.

336
00:22:40,231 --> 00:22:41,646
Pro Vee?

337
00:22:41,670 --> 00:22:44,894
No way.
Pro Vee would never do that.

338
00:22:45,077 --> 00:22:46,569
If anyone's suspicious,

339
00:22:46,594 --> 00:22:48,340
it's Pro Jin.

340
00:22:48,570 --> 00:22:50,249
She used to work at that course.

341
00:22:50,274 --> 00:22:52,741
She could've come here to get
information about our course

342
00:22:52,766 --> 00:22:54,520
and pass it on to them.

343
00:23:04,662 --> 00:23:07,109
I didn't think
you'd take it this far.

344
00:23:07,134 --> 00:23:08,371
You've got some nerve.

345
00:23:10,702 --> 00:23:12,438
I told you.

346
00:23:12,463 --> 00:23:15,692
If I'm going to do something,
I'm going all the way.

347
00:23:17,002 --> 00:23:20,550
That's how you play the game
in business.

348
00:23:21,296 --> 00:23:23,026
The weak lose.

349
00:23:23,818 --> 00:23:27,856
Only the strong
get to have it all.

350
00:23:29,818 --> 00:23:32,156
With results like these,

351
00:23:33,124 --> 00:23:34,870
don't I deserve a little bonus?

352
00:23:50,465 --> 00:23:52,321
- Pro Vee.
- Hmm?

353
00:23:52,488 --> 00:23:54,345
There's something
I want to ask you.

354
00:23:55,417 --> 00:23:56,466
What is it?

355
00:24:00,259 --> 00:24:03,623
You know our course is being
sabotaged, right?

356
00:24:04,130 --> 00:24:07,216
Mm. I've heard about it
from some of the staff.

357
00:24:07,352 --> 00:24:08,765
Is there anything
I can help with?

358
00:24:22,421 --> 00:24:27,077
Someone said they saw you
at The Royal Green.

359
00:24:27,599 --> 00:24:29,217
- So I wanted to...
- Yes.

360
00:24:29,242 --> 00:24:31,805
Ms. Yupadee, the owner,
asked me to meet with her.

361
00:24:33,166 --> 00:24:35,860
Can I ask what you talked about?

362
00:24:37,208 --> 00:24:39,452
She asked me
to teach at her course.

363
00:24:39,509 --> 00:24:42,183
She even offered to pay me more.

364
00:24:44,758 --> 00:24:47,013
Oh. I see.

365
00:24:50,053 --> 00:24:51,424
Is something wrong?

366
00:24:54,831 --> 00:24:57,564
People at the course think

367
00:24:57,589 --> 00:25:00,645
The Royal Green
is behind all of this

368
00:25:00,805 --> 00:25:03,038
to discredit our course.

369
00:25:03,063 --> 00:25:06,533
So they think
I might be involved.

370
00:25:07,958 --> 00:25:09,212
That's not true.

371
00:25:09,585 --> 00:25:12,681
- We're trying to find out...
- Do you think I am?

372
00:25:21,150 --> 00:25:23,425
If it wasn't Pro Vee, who else
do you think it could be?

373
00:25:23,450 --> 00:25:25,450
- Pro Jin.
- Are you crazy?

374
00:25:27,366 --> 00:25:29,114
You used to work there.

375
00:25:29,139 --> 00:25:31,306
And when I asked you
to join this course,

376
00:25:31,331 --> 00:25:33,054
you moved here right away.

377
00:25:33,987 --> 00:25:35,738
I may look cold and intimidating,

378
00:25:35,763 --> 00:25:38,353
but I would never do
something that ridiculous.

379
00:25:38,378 --> 00:25:41,317
And I hate people
who play dirty.

380
00:25:41,342 --> 00:25:43,753
What do you mean by "play dirty"?

381
00:25:44,859 --> 00:25:47,028
Your boss's favorite pro.

382
00:25:47,053 --> 00:25:48,427
She may have a pretty face,

383
00:25:48,452 --> 00:25:50,660
but who would've thought
she'd do something like that?

384
00:25:50,685 --> 00:25:53,457
Do something like what?
What exactly do you mean?

385
00:25:53,691 --> 00:25:55,316
What? Tell me.

386
00:25:57,734 --> 00:26:00,654
Wait, Vee.
That's not what I meant.

387
00:26:00,776 --> 00:26:01,871
It's not like that.

388
00:26:01,896 --> 00:26:03,252
I was just telling you...

389
00:26:03,277 --> 00:26:04,498
But the reason you told me

390
00:26:05,098 --> 00:26:06,908
because you wanted to know

391
00:26:06,933 --> 00:26:08,488
if I did it, didn't you?

392
00:26:09,219 --> 00:26:10,854
That's not what I meant.

393
00:26:11,189 --> 00:26:12,708
I really didn't think that.

394
00:26:12,733 --> 00:26:14,607
I'll sleep in
my own room tonight.

395
00:26:15,027 --> 00:26:16,083
Otherwise,

396
00:26:16,965 --> 00:26:18,524
you might not trust me.

397
00:26:18,628 --> 00:26:22,421
No, that's not it.
Please, believe me.

398
00:26:22,446 --> 00:26:24,261
I really didn't think that.

399
00:26:27,359 --> 00:26:29,979
I never thought you'd do
something like that, Vee.

400
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:32,050
Belle told me

401
00:26:32,075 --> 00:26:35,444
that Pro Jin saw you
at that course,

402
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:39,909
so everyone started
putting the pieces together...

403
00:26:45,175 --> 00:26:48,293
Then why did you and Pro Vee
have the same coach back then?

404
00:26:48,825 --> 00:26:50,983
It's not complicated.
I couldn't afford one.

405
00:26:51,886 --> 00:26:54,277
My family didn't really support
me playing golf.

406
00:26:54,467 --> 00:26:57,540
Vee knew that, so she offered
to share her coach with me.

407
00:26:57,834 --> 00:26:59,788
Just having Pro Vee's coach
come over

408
00:26:59,813 --> 00:27:01,653
and coach you during the match

409
00:27:01,678 --> 00:27:03,149
was enough
to get you disqualified?

410
00:27:03,174 --> 00:27:06,392
According to the rules, a golfer
can't receive advice from anyone

411
00:27:06,417 --> 00:27:08,012
other than their own caddie.

412
00:27:08,403 --> 00:27:10,823
If someone tells them the line,
how to hit the shot,

413
00:27:10,848 --> 00:27:12,390
or interferes
with their decisions,

414
00:27:12,414 --> 00:27:15,027
the golfer
is penalized immediately.

415
00:27:15,290 --> 00:27:17,387
But why would the coach do that

416
00:27:17,412 --> 00:27:19,230
when he knew the rules so well?

417
00:27:20,192 --> 00:27:22,751
Exactly. What else
am I supposed to think?

418
00:27:23,330 --> 00:27:26,552
And Venus won that match
just like she wanted.

419
00:27:29,051 --> 00:27:32,205
What if the coach did it
without Pro Vee knowing?

420
00:27:34,086 --> 00:27:35,396
Don't be so naive.

421
00:27:36,017 --> 00:27:38,542
He must've known that
if I made it to the final hole,

422
00:27:38,828 --> 00:27:40,352
I'd definitely
have the highest score.

423
00:27:41,638 --> 00:27:46,446
So you think Pro Vee was involved
in discrediting our course.

424
00:27:46,822 --> 00:27:48,903
Someone who's done something
like that before

425
00:27:48,928 --> 00:27:50,476
could certainly do it again.

426
00:27:51,717 --> 00:27:54,844
She might've even taken
a big payout from them.

427
00:28:06,303 --> 00:28:08,287
I'm sorry, Vee.

428
00:28:18,924 --> 00:28:22,278
Don't cry. I believe you now.
I believe you.

429
00:28:28,932 --> 00:28:30,747
It's okay. Don't cry.

430
00:28:44,355 --> 00:28:46,433
Let me tell you this, Nana.

431
00:28:46,822 --> 00:28:50,553
If there's anyone in this world
who wants the best for you,

432
00:28:51,089 --> 00:28:52,821
I'll always be one of them.

433
00:28:55,646 --> 00:28:57,052
I know.

434
00:28:57,866 --> 00:29:01,884
I told everyone that you'd never
do something like that.

435
00:29:02,189 --> 00:29:03,637
If anyone's suspicious,

436
00:29:03,662 --> 00:29:05,215
it's Pro Jin.

437
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:08,685
No, don't. Don't accuse people
like that without proof.

438
00:29:11,910 --> 00:29:15,058
Nut said the evidence has already
been sent for testing.

439
00:29:15,083 --> 00:29:18,180
We'll know the truth soon, okay?

440
00:29:21,101 --> 00:29:23,821
Come on, don't cry.

441
00:29:23,846 --> 00:29:25,846
You're an executive now.

442
00:29:26,028 --> 00:29:28,485
How can you sit here
crying your eyes out like this?

443
00:29:28,835 --> 00:29:30,835
You'll lose all your credibility.

444
00:29:34,812 --> 00:29:38,049
Don't cry. Come here.

445
00:29:42,625 --> 00:29:43,882
That's enough now.

446
00:33:17,775 --> 00:33:20,019
As I promised everyone,

447
00:33:20,044 --> 00:33:22,576
we've looked into the wastewater
in the community

448
00:33:22,601 --> 00:33:24,508
to find out what caused it.

449
00:33:24,533 --> 00:33:27,218
But first, I'd like to explain

450
00:33:27,243 --> 00:33:29,329
that our course has
a wastewater treatment system

451
00:33:29,354 --> 00:33:31,380
before any water is discharged
into the waterway.

452
00:33:31,405 --> 00:33:33,485
We also carefully select our
fertilizers and other chemicals.

453
00:33:33,510 --> 00:33:36,113
We only use environmentally
friendly products.

454
00:33:38,441 --> 00:33:39,552
Environmentally friendly?

455
00:33:39,955 --> 00:33:41,678
Then how do you explain
all those dead fish?

456
00:33:41,703 --> 00:33:43,035
Yeah, exactly.

457
00:33:43,575 --> 00:33:46,504
The dead fish in the water
weren't native fish.

458
00:33:46,529 --> 00:33:49,686
They were marine fish
planted there to stage the scene.

459
00:33:49,711 --> 00:33:51,575
As for the smell,

460
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:54,064
someone poured chemicals
around the area.

461
00:33:54,089 --> 00:33:57,302
They don't harm the waterway.
They only cause a bad smell.

462
00:33:57,770 --> 00:34:01,697
Today, I have invited experts
from the relevant authorities

463
00:34:01,722 --> 00:34:03,722
to explain everything
to everyone.

464
00:34:04,193 --> 00:34:05,232
Please, go ahead.

465
00:34:10,761 --> 00:34:12,358
As you can see,

466
00:34:12,383 --> 00:34:14,801
this is a water sample
taken from the community canal,

467
00:34:14,841 --> 00:34:16,615
and this is a sample
from the holding pond

468
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:18,215
where the course
discharges its water.

469
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:21,662
Our tests found
that the community's water

470
00:34:21,687 --> 00:34:23,687
has a COD, or Chemical Oxygen...

471
00:34:51,490 --> 00:34:53,829
I actually know a thing or two
about hotel operations.

472
00:34:54,881 --> 00:34:57,444
Maybe next time I could help you
with your work in Chiang Rai?

473
00:34:57,603 --> 00:34:59,603
Let's save this course first.

474
00:34:59,994 --> 00:35:03,990
So, who are you sending
to represent our course

475
00:35:04,015 --> 00:35:06,015
in the All Star
Women's Golf Tournament?

476
00:35:06,269 --> 00:35:07,590
I've already got a plan.

477
00:35:08,415 --> 00:35:10,789
Our course is definitely
taking home the championship.

478
00:35:12,507 --> 00:35:13,686
Don't get ahead of yourself.

479
00:35:16,751 --> 00:35:18,466
If something goes wrong,

480
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:20,777
I don't want to hear
your excuses afterward.

481
00:35:41,971 --> 00:35:43,343
Who should I put up against her?

482
00:35:45,018 --> 00:35:46,438
The pros here are all lousy.

483
00:36:02,075 --> 00:36:03,420
Don't worry.

484
00:36:03,445 --> 00:36:06,771
Even though what happened
wasn't caused by our course,

485
00:36:06,796 --> 00:36:08,703
we're still
part of the same community.

486
00:36:08,728 --> 00:36:11,062
People from the community
work here with us,

487
00:36:11,087 --> 00:36:13,390
and we rely on
the community, too.

488
00:36:13,415 --> 00:36:15,784
My grandfather and father
always told me

489
00:36:15,809 --> 00:36:17,442
that we're
part of this community.

490
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:19,206
We can't stand on our own.

491
00:36:19,230 --> 00:36:21,725
So Goodview Golf Club

492
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:24,251
will work with
the relevant authorities

493
00:36:24,276 --> 00:36:26,258
until everything
returns to normal.

494
00:36:26,305 --> 00:36:29,016
And we'll cover
all the expenses ourselves.

495
00:36:31,734 --> 00:36:34,285
Thank you. Thank you so much,
Goodview Golf Club.

496
00:36:34,318 --> 00:36:36,222
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

497
00:36:44,739 --> 00:36:49,250
We're sorry for the things
we said to you earlier.

498
00:36:49,914 --> 00:36:52,683
If there's anything the community
needs, please let us know.

499
00:36:52,708 --> 00:36:54,359
We're all on the same side.

500
00:37:09,486 --> 00:37:13,275
Looks like you won't be able
to escape this course after all.

501
00:37:17,883 --> 00:37:19,927
Miss Nana, stop right there.

502
00:37:20,070 --> 00:37:22,070
Come with me.
We've got a problem.

503
00:37:22,095 --> 00:37:23,460
What's wrong, Chef?

504
00:37:29,086 --> 00:37:31,543
Ton, what happened?

505
00:37:31,568 --> 00:37:34,264
Don't tell me you did
something to Ton and then he...

506
00:37:34,289 --> 00:37:36,689
Hold on. I didn't do anything
to him. Nothing inappropriate.

507
00:37:36,714 --> 00:37:38,811
He's handsome, sure,
but I've already got my masseur.

508
00:37:38,836 --> 00:37:40,200
I wouldn't do
something like that.

509
00:37:41,402 --> 00:37:44,619
Ton came to confess that he knows
who's behind

510
00:37:44,644 --> 00:37:47,254
the smear campaign
against our golf course.

511
00:37:48,407 --> 00:37:52,630
I was the one who took
our course's food packaging

512
00:37:52,655 --> 00:37:55,995
and gave it to Mr. March
at The Royal Green.

513
00:37:56,995 --> 00:37:59,304
You can punish me
however you want.

514
00:37:59,329 --> 00:38:01,329
Just please don't fire me.

515
00:38:01,486 --> 00:38:03,688
I really had no choice, Miss.

516
00:38:03,713 --> 00:38:07,148
I... I really needed the money.

517
00:38:08,055 --> 00:38:09,726
You have
no loyalty to this course.

518
00:38:09,751 --> 00:38:12,426
And were you the one who posted
those lies about our course

519
00:38:12,450 --> 00:38:15,159
and my restaurant, too?

520
00:38:15,184 --> 00:38:16,866
You've caused me
real damage, Ton.

521
00:38:16,891 --> 00:38:20,751
No, I didn't. But I know
Mr. March's people did it.

522
00:38:20,909 --> 00:38:23,168
It was the people who left
our course to work there.

523
00:38:23,193 --> 00:38:25,481
And as for the dead fish
and that rotten smell,

524
00:38:25,506 --> 00:38:26,808
Mr. March was behind those, too.

525
00:38:27,831 --> 00:38:29,212
I knew it.

526
00:38:29,581 --> 00:38:32,177
That bastard March,
that rotten relative!

527
00:38:33,505 --> 00:38:34,624
Are you calling me rotten?

528
00:38:35,952 --> 00:38:37,032
Ohhh... you mean March!

529
00:38:38,158 --> 00:38:41,430
Miss Nana, please calm down.
I already questioned Ton.

530
00:38:41,582 --> 00:38:43,712
He had his reasons.
He really needed the money.

531
00:38:43,737 --> 00:38:45,539
His younger brother
is about to start school,

532
00:38:45,595 --> 00:38:47,570
and on top of that,
his mother got sick.

533
00:38:50,642 --> 00:38:53,357
When we're talking money
with someone who really needs it,

534
00:38:54,016 --> 00:38:55,762
I understand.

535
00:38:56,789 --> 00:38:58,226
I'm sorry, Miss Nana.

536
00:38:59,034 --> 00:39:00,054
It's okay.

537
00:39:00,395 --> 00:39:03,510
The root of the problem is
the community's quality of life.

538
00:39:04,034 --> 00:39:06,488
When people
are desperate for money,

539
00:39:06,702 --> 00:39:09,165
we end up letting money
have power over us.

540
00:39:10,614 --> 00:39:12,473
I'm actually working on
a scholarship program

541
00:39:12,498 --> 00:39:14,396
for kids in the community.

542
00:39:14,420 --> 00:39:17,071
Go talk to Belle. She'll tell you
what you need to do.

543
00:39:17,096 --> 00:39:19,205
And when it comes to healthcare
for the community,

544
00:39:19,230 --> 00:39:21,844
we'll arrange for a mobile
medical unit to come here.

545
00:39:21,869 --> 00:39:24,437
We can use our course
as a clinic once a month.

546
00:39:24,462 --> 00:39:25,971
Let's do it on our day off.

547
00:39:26,170 --> 00:39:27,796
Thank you so much, Miss Nana.

548
00:39:29,718 --> 00:39:33,429
And if you're ever in trouble
again, come talk to us.

549
00:39:33,454 --> 00:39:36,410
I see everyone at this course
as family.

550
00:39:36,561 --> 00:39:38,561
I won't tell anyone this time,

551
00:39:38,586 --> 00:39:40,456
but I'll put you on probation.

552
00:39:40,481 --> 00:39:43,425
If it happens again,
I won't forgive you.

553
00:39:44,012 --> 00:39:45,020
Yes, Miss.

554
00:39:45,510 --> 00:39:47,026
Now go. Get back to work.

555
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:49,581
Love this course
the way it loves you, okay?

556
00:39:50,915 --> 00:39:52,323
Thank you, Miss Nana.

557
00:40:01,409 --> 00:40:05,526
Miss Nana, what are we gonna do
about that Royal Green gang?

558
00:40:05,551 --> 00:40:06,675
We need to make them pay.

559
00:40:06,699 --> 00:40:09,170
You can't just
go soft on them, Miss Nana.

560
00:40:09,670 --> 00:40:11,643
Chef, poop stinks.

561
00:40:11,668 --> 00:40:13,692
Then don't mess with it.
Don't go near it.

562
00:40:13,717 --> 00:40:15,448
There's so much good stuff
we can create here,

563
00:40:15,473 --> 00:40:17,408
so much positive energy
to put into it.

564
00:40:17,433 --> 00:40:19,595
Let's not waste our time
on things like this.

565
00:40:19,620 --> 00:40:20,885
I'm not letting them off.

566
00:40:20,909 --> 00:40:23,804
But I'd rather leave it
to the authorities to deal with.

567
00:40:23,990 --> 00:40:28,548
Whoa! The light of virtue
is shining right behind you!

568
00:40:28,573 --> 00:40:31,051
A saint has descended upon us!
Everything's divine!

569
00:40:31,076 --> 00:40:34,643
Let me bow to you.
Come on... whew!

570
00:40:43,439 --> 00:40:44,471
Nut.

571
00:40:47,011 --> 00:40:48,157
Have a seat.

572
00:40:50,685 --> 00:40:53,472
Do you think
everything that's happened

573
00:40:53,497 --> 00:40:55,624
was the Royal Green's doing?

574
00:40:55,648 --> 00:40:56,766
It's possible.

575
00:40:57,030 --> 00:41:00,161
If they did it,
what do they want?

576
00:41:00,303 --> 00:41:02,083
I knew Ms. Yupadee before.

577
00:41:05,114 --> 00:41:06,377
Very well.

578
00:41:07,138 --> 00:41:08,726
Did you two ever hook up?

579
00:41:10,083 --> 00:41:11,506
- Mm-hmm.
- Ooh!

580
00:41:12,069 --> 00:41:13,651
I was just kidding.

581
00:41:16,919 --> 00:41:19,769
Ms. Yupadee
is a ruthless businesswoman.

582
00:41:19,794 --> 00:41:21,853
She drives other businesses
into the ground,

583
00:41:21,878 --> 00:41:25,068
then swoops in and offers to buy
them for as little as possible.

584
00:41:26,951 --> 00:41:28,923
You call that helping?

585
00:41:28,948 --> 00:41:32,162
That's what she did to the hotel
I used to work at in Chiang Rai.

586
00:41:32,190 --> 00:41:34,143
She used me as one of her pawns.

587
00:41:35,429 --> 00:41:38,162
So she wants our golf course?

588
00:41:38,383 --> 00:41:40,214
For as little
as she can get it for.

589
00:41:40,618 --> 00:41:44,017
She'll run us into the ground
until we're forced to sell.

590
00:41:44,815 --> 00:41:46,680
That's not very creative.

591
00:41:46,934 --> 00:41:51,125
She'll use her charm,
her tricks, her money...

592
00:41:51,150 --> 00:41:54,526
anything she has
to get what she wants,

593
00:41:54,551 --> 00:41:56,322
without caring who she hurts.

594
00:41:56,369 --> 00:42:00,055
If we're going up against her,
you need to be very careful.

595
00:42:01,642 --> 00:42:03,934
I'll fight her with something
she doesn't have.

596
00:42:05,458 --> 00:42:06,513
What's that?

597
00:42:08,010 --> 00:42:09,718
- Goodness.
- Whoa.

598
00:42:11,244 --> 00:42:13,005
Don't laugh at me yet, Nut.

599
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:14,565
I'm not being naive.

600
00:42:14,629 --> 00:42:18,646
I believe goodness, sincerity,
and a positive attitude

601
00:42:18,671 --> 00:42:21,230
can help us find a way through
almost any problem.

602
00:42:21,246 --> 00:42:22,762
Just look at
what happened this time.

603
00:42:22,930 --> 00:42:24,956
Not only did they
fail to frame us,

604
00:42:24,981 --> 00:42:27,512
they actually helped us regain
the community's trust.

605
00:42:28,718 --> 00:42:31,464
Now that's a modern CEO.

606
00:42:31,489 --> 00:42:35,219
Guess you'll be back in France
in less than six months, then.

607
00:42:40,094 --> 00:42:43,497
Oh, and what about the All Star
Women's Golf Tournament?

608
00:42:43,947 --> 00:42:45,509
I've already worked out a plan.

609
00:42:45,534 --> 00:42:47,534
I'll present it
at tomorrow's meeting.

610
00:42:47,777 --> 00:42:49,514
What about you, Nana?

611
00:42:49,539 --> 00:42:52,260
Have you decided who you'll
nominate to represent our course?

612
00:42:52,356 --> 00:42:53,460
I have.

613
00:42:57,790 --> 00:43:02,183
Do you think Goodview will
send you to represent the course?

614
00:43:02,809 --> 00:43:06,356
If they have to choose one,
it'll probably be Pro Vee.

615
00:43:07,461 --> 00:43:08,795
I've followed the news.

616
00:43:09,570 --> 00:43:12,197
You almost won,
but were penalized and lost.

617
00:43:13,085 --> 00:43:15,692
Two best friends had to face
each other in the tournament...

618
00:43:15,717 --> 00:43:16,779
What do you want?

619
00:43:21,287 --> 00:43:22,596
Come back to our course.

620
00:43:23,159 --> 00:43:25,275
And I'll make sure you're the one
who represents us.

621
00:43:26,610 --> 00:43:28,086
I believe

622
00:43:28,111 --> 00:43:31,079
a pro like you could beat Pro Vee
any day.

623
00:43:31,378 --> 00:43:33,688
The pros from the other courses
are nothing special.

624
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:35,466
Don't you agree, Pro?

625
00:43:46,995 --> 00:43:50,737
Four months have already flown by
since I took over the course.

626
00:43:50,762 --> 00:43:53,182
And business has been
getting better and better.

627
00:43:53,207 --> 00:43:56,774
Who knows? We might even
turn a profit this quarter.

628
00:43:56,799 --> 00:43:58,981
All thanks to this young CEO.

629
00:44:00,269 --> 00:44:02,203
Mr. Sanchai must be thrilled.

630
00:44:02,543 --> 00:44:06,069
And you might get to go back to
France sooner than you expected.

631
00:44:06,951 --> 00:44:09,455
You deserves some credit, too.

632
00:44:10,140 --> 00:44:11,757
Mm. No, that's not right.

633
00:44:11,782 --> 00:44:16,247
Everyone at the course
helped bring it back to life.

634
00:44:18,209 --> 00:44:20,657
You're quite capable, Nana.
You know that?

635
00:44:21,899 --> 00:44:25,305
And your sincerity
and straightforwardness

636
00:44:25,330 --> 00:44:27,330
have really won everyone over.

637
00:44:27,814 --> 00:44:30,133
Including you, right?

638
00:44:33,994 --> 00:44:36,752
Oh, there's one more thing.
I was going to tell you then,

639
00:44:36,777 --> 00:44:38,390
but then all that happened.

640
00:44:38,415 --> 00:44:40,226
The Golf Course Network

641
00:44:40,251 --> 00:44:42,315
is organizing the All Star
Women's Golf Tournament.

642
00:44:42,339 --> 00:44:45,422
Each course will send one golfer
to represent them.

643
00:44:45,447 --> 00:44:47,645
The golfer
from the winning course

644
00:44:47,670 --> 00:44:50,062
will earn the right to host
the Asian Tour,

645
00:44:50,087 --> 00:44:52,379
which is a huge event
at the end of the year.

646
00:44:52,698 --> 00:44:56,939
So I was thinking of sending you
to represent Goodview.

647
00:44:57,803 --> 00:44:59,812
We have plenty of good pros here.

648
00:44:59,837 --> 00:45:01,058
Send someone else.

649
00:45:01,479 --> 00:45:04,273
No. It has to be you, Vee.

650
00:45:04,806 --> 00:45:06,811
I had Belle look into everyone.

651
00:45:06,836 --> 00:45:08,637
You're the best choice.

652
00:45:08,955 --> 00:45:10,422
I'd rather not compete.

653
00:45:10,883 --> 00:45:14,810
Why not? Please, Vee.
Represent our course.

654
00:45:16,312 --> 00:45:17,351
No.

655
00:45:17,909 --> 00:45:19,657
I haven't competed
in a long time.

656
00:45:19,682 --> 00:45:21,982
And I don't plan on
competing again.

657
00:45:22,461 --> 00:45:23,517
Why not?

658
00:45:24,846 --> 00:45:26,776
There are some things
I'd rather not explain.

659
00:45:29,402 --> 00:45:30,906
I'm not feeling well lately.

660
00:45:30,931 --> 00:45:33,719
I'll sleep in my room tonight.

661
00:45:33,744 --> 00:45:34,878
So you don't catch it.

662
00:46:09,570 --> 00:46:10,592
Can I shower with you?

663
00:46:13,032 --> 00:46:14,183
Sure.

664
00:49:05,129 --> 00:49:07,379
I'm moving back
to the Royal Green.

665
00:49:12,968 --> 00:49:14,999
Have you gotten
all the information you needed?

666
00:49:18,566 --> 00:49:21,967
You'd be disappointed in me
if I did something like that.

667
00:49:22,509 --> 00:49:25,861
Not really. Everyone probably
has their own reasons.

668
00:49:26,639 --> 00:49:28,308
But I'd be very disappointed

669
00:49:28,333 --> 00:49:30,593
if I were involved in something
like this.

670
00:49:32,136 --> 00:49:33,794
So you're saying
you didn't do it.

671
00:49:34,782 --> 00:49:36,743
Then why go back there?

672
00:49:37,314 --> 00:49:39,314
Because I want to
matter for once.

673
00:49:40,106 --> 00:49:42,470
I want to prove myself.

674
00:49:42,495 --> 00:49:44,201
Prove I'm just
as good as Pro Vee.

675
00:49:57,738 --> 00:49:58,767
- Hey.
- Hmm?

676
00:49:58,792 --> 00:50:00,275
I brought you something today.

677
00:50:00,961 --> 00:50:02,770
- Let me guess.
- Go ahead.

678
00:50:03,098 --> 00:50:05,129
- What is it?
- Cake?

679
00:50:05,154 --> 00:50:07,330
- No way. Wrong.
- Then let's just open it.

680
00:50:07,355 --> 00:50:08,782
- Go on.
- Oh!

681
00:50:08,806 --> 00:50:10,240
Celadon from Chiang Mai.

682
00:50:10,265 --> 00:50:12,096
Whoa, pottery!

683
00:50:12,121 --> 00:50:13,161
Hey, look.

684
00:50:13,185 --> 00:50:14,427
Rub it three times
and a genie pops out.

685
00:50:14,452 --> 00:50:16,653
- I know exactly what this is.
- No, just put it away.

686
00:50:18,696 --> 00:50:20,910
- Thanks, buddy. Really, thanks.
- Sure.

687
00:50:21,630 --> 00:50:23,533
Your daughter's really something.

688
00:50:23,558 --> 00:50:25,126
She's been
doing all sorts of things.

689
00:50:25,150 --> 00:50:26,527
She's changed everything.

690
00:50:26,959 --> 00:50:29,507
Yeah, she really has.
My wife and kids love it, too.

691
00:50:29,532 --> 00:50:32,198
They have so much to do
while they're waiting for me.

692
00:50:32,262 --> 00:50:36,919
Look, you don't need to worry
about your daughter's abilities.

693
00:50:36,943 --> 00:50:38,765
Just look at me. See?

694
00:50:38,789 --> 00:50:40,329
She's got it all
from her old man.

695
00:50:40,354 --> 00:50:41,974
Yeah, that's true.

696
00:50:41,999 --> 00:50:46,578
Hey, have you told your kids yet
about the cancer?

697
00:50:48,885 --> 00:50:50,687
Not yet. I don't have the heart
to tell them.

698
00:50:50,712 --> 00:50:52,464
I'm afraid
it'll only make things worse.

699
00:50:53,237 --> 00:50:55,495
I had her come back to help out

700
00:50:55,520 --> 00:50:57,264
so she'd get familiar
with the business.

701
00:50:58,329 --> 00:51:00,332
If something
happens to me someday,

702
00:51:01,168 --> 00:51:02,937
she'll be ready to take over.

703
00:51:02,962 --> 00:51:05,783
Come on. You're talking like
you're about to die.

704
00:51:05,808 --> 00:51:08,293
There are so many ways
to treat cancer nowadays.

705
00:51:08,318 --> 00:51:09,372
Don't be scared.

706
00:51:11,675 --> 00:51:16,412
I think you should start
the chemo the doctor recommended.

707
00:51:16,624 --> 00:51:18,660
The sooner you start,
the sooner you'll get better.

708
00:51:22,926 --> 00:51:24,603
I think
I need a little more time.

709
00:51:25,365 --> 00:51:26,878
I just need some time
to process it.

710
00:51:28,338 --> 00:51:30,743
Either way,
you need to tell your kids.

711
00:51:31,354 --> 00:51:32,678
- Yeah, I agree.
- Mm-hmm.

712
00:51:32,703 --> 00:51:35,203
- Here, eat.
- Come on.

713
00:51:40,535 --> 00:51:43,846
Miss Nana, I had an urgent matter
to take care of this morning.

714
00:51:43,871 --> 00:51:45,568
I'll come into the office
this afternoon.

715
00:51:50,801 --> 00:51:52,221
You seem to be in a hurry.

716
00:51:54,375 --> 00:51:55,856
I guess
it doesn't matter to anyone

717
00:51:55,881 --> 00:51:57,618
whether I'm here or not.

718
00:52:03,297 --> 00:52:05,378
You may not matter
to some people,

719
00:52:05,982 --> 00:52:08,259
but that doesn't mean
you don't matter to anyone.

720
00:52:10,058 --> 00:52:13,243
Me? Matter to someone?

721
00:52:13,997 --> 00:52:15,108
I doubt it.

722
00:52:18,705 --> 00:52:20,100
Don't say that.

723
00:52:21,188 --> 00:52:23,188
You're not just hurting yourself.

724
00:52:24,389 --> 00:52:28,025
You're also insulting the people
who care about you.

725
00:52:31,912 --> 00:52:34,836
I'm off. I don't like goodbyes.

726
00:52:39,178 --> 00:52:40,968
I don't like them either.

727
00:52:44,427 --> 00:52:45,730
Then let's not say goodbye.

728
00:52:48,790 --> 00:52:49,893
No goodbyes.

729
00:52:50,566 --> 00:52:52,043
Just don't forget about us.

730
00:53:21,058 --> 00:53:22,772
Perfect, Nut. This is spot-on.

731
00:53:22,796 --> 00:53:24,951
Everyone's going to
love our course.

732
00:53:26,059 --> 00:53:28,202
And have you decided
who'll represent our course?

733
00:53:28,227 --> 00:53:29,710
Who did you choose, Nana?

734
00:53:30,296 --> 00:53:32,382
I'll make
the final decision soon.

735
00:53:32,908 --> 00:53:34,122
Mm, sounds good.

736
00:53:34,289 --> 00:53:37,401
We also need to take profile
photos of everyone competing.

737
00:53:37,950 --> 00:53:40,379
- Sure.
- Okay. Thank you.

738
00:53:57,717 --> 00:54:01,607
Miss Nana, Pro Jin has notified
HR that she's resigning.

739
00:54:03,329 --> 00:54:06,361
Why? Belle, what happened?
Do you know?

740
00:54:10,987 --> 00:54:12,939
Pro Jin wants to
represent a course

741
00:54:12,964 --> 00:54:15,471
in the upcoming
All Star tournament.

742
00:54:15,662 --> 00:54:18,635
The Royal Green happened
to offer her the opportunity,

743
00:54:18,897 --> 00:54:20,231
so she left.

744
00:54:22,586 --> 00:54:24,960
I didn't even think of that.

745
00:54:25,293 --> 00:54:28,138
If I were her,
I'd probably feel hurt, too.

746
00:54:30,327 --> 00:54:33,278
And she wants to
compete against Pro Vee

747
00:54:33,303 --> 00:54:36,080
to prove she's every bit
as good as her.

748
00:54:37,934 --> 00:54:39,460
What do you mean, Belle?

749
00:54:39,485 --> 00:54:41,485
She believes Pro Vee cheated her.

750
00:54:43,278 --> 00:54:46,560
She was disqualified before
the competition even ended.

751
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:51,219
She believes that if she'd
made it to the 18th hole,

752
00:54:51,244 --> 00:54:54,076
Pro Vee wouldn't have been
the one to win that match.

753
00:54:55,248 --> 00:54:58,120
- Pro Vee cheated her?
- Yes.

754
00:54:58,467 --> 00:55:00,737
Afterward, Pro Vee must've
felt ashamed of a victory

755
00:55:00,762 --> 00:55:03,157
she'd cheated her way to.

756
00:55:03,193 --> 00:55:04,566
So she quit competing

757
00:55:04,591 --> 00:55:06,456
and became
a golf instructor instead.

758
00:55:25,218 --> 00:55:26,535
Hello, Auntie.

759
00:55:28,273 --> 00:55:31,386
Nana! What brings you here, kid?

760
00:55:34,819 --> 00:55:38,600
What happened that day has
stayed with Vee all this time.

761
00:55:39,993 --> 00:55:42,138
It was
the final day of the tournament.

762
00:55:43,042 --> 00:55:44,200
Vee and Jin...

763
00:55:44,582 --> 00:55:46,706
had always trained together.

764
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:50,659
Their scores
had been neck and neck,

765
00:55:51,487 --> 00:55:53,792
but Jin was disqualified
for breaking the rules.

766
00:55:54,562 --> 00:55:58,803
So Vee's score
put her among the leaders,

767
00:56:00,234 --> 00:56:01,793
with a real shot at the title.

768
00:56:02,991 --> 00:56:06,930
But then her father had
a heart attack.

769
00:56:08,297 --> 00:56:09,970
He had to be rushed
to the hospital.

770
00:56:10,957 --> 00:56:15,458
At that point,
Vee had only three holes left.

771
00:56:18,877 --> 00:56:22,044
We thought
it wasn't anything too serious,

772
00:56:22,045 --> 00:56:23,846
so we told Vee to keep playing,

773
00:56:23,871 --> 00:56:25,785
while I rushed to the hospital.

774
00:56:26,571 --> 00:56:30,058
At first,
Vee wasn't sure what to do.

775
00:56:30,657 --> 00:56:31,868
But in the end...

776
00:56:37,270 --> 00:56:39,533
she chose to stay
and finish the game

777
00:56:39,558 --> 00:56:41,422
instead of going to her father.

778
00:56:49,526 --> 00:56:51,677
By the time
Vee got to the hospital,

779
00:56:53,328 --> 00:56:54,685
it was too late.

780
00:56:57,523 --> 00:57:02,326
Her father was gone,
and Vee never got to say goodbye.

781
00:57:05,884 --> 00:57:06,963
Vee...

782
00:58:00,192 --> 00:58:04,585
Her father was gone,
and Vee never got to say goodbye.

783
00:58:08,383 --> 00:58:11,675
Vee blamed herself
for choosing golf

784
00:58:11,700 --> 00:58:13,700
instead of going to her father.

785
00:58:15,657 --> 00:58:20,172
From then on,
she never competed again.

786
00:58:24,097 --> 00:58:27,055
But Vee still plays golf.

787
00:58:29,077 --> 00:58:31,630
Vee loves golf.

788
00:58:32,746 --> 00:58:35,246
It was her only dream
since she was a child.

789
00:58:38,427 --> 00:58:40,062
But after what happened,

790
00:58:41,181 --> 00:58:44,843
Vee turned away from competition

791
00:58:46,174 --> 00:58:51,570
and chose to stay in golf
only as an instructor.

792
00:58:55,344 --> 00:58:56,460
And...

793
00:58:58,637 --> 00:59:00,637
What about
Pro Jin's disqualification?

794
00:59:01,204 --> 00:59:03,021
Was it because of Vee's coach?

795
00:59:27,178 --> 00:59:28,185
Pro Vee.

796
00:59:31,260 --> 00:59:33,450
There's something
I want to talk to you about.

797
00:59:33,929 --> 00:59:36,279
If this is about
the All Star tournament,

798
00:59:36,304 --> 00:59:37,652
don't waste your time.

799
00:59:39,951 --> 00:59:41,723
I know everything now.

800
00:59:43,169 --> 00:59:45,676
About your father
and the coach who...

801
00:59:45,701 --> 00:59:46,942
Who told you?

802
00:59:54,002 --> 00:59:55,349
That doesn't matter.

803
00:59:55,865 --> 00:59:59,303
What matters is that
you're running away from it.

804
01:00:00,062 --> 01:00:01,750
You think I'm running away?

805
01:00:03,411 --> 01:00:04,498
Yes.

806
01:00:07,910 --> 01:00:11,649
Don't let your past
dictate the path of your dreams.

807
01:00:12,824 --> 01:00:15,474
The coach I trusted
made my friend

808
01:00:15,499 --> 01:00:17,892
leave the competition
right before my eyes.

809
01:00:19,518 --> 01:00:21,870
And I didn't make it in time
to say goodbye to my father

810
01:00:22,256 --> 01:00:24,073
because I chose
to finish the game.

811
01:00:24,391 --> 01:00:26,369
How do you think I should feel

812
01:00:26,394 --> 01:00:28,761
about a victory
I earned that way?

813
01:00:28,786 --> 01:00:30,972
So you never competed again

814
01:00:30,997 --> 01:00:32,686
because of what happened
that day?

815
01:00:35,451 --> 01:00:38,034
That's exactly
why I want you to compete.

816
01:00:38,485 --> 01:00:40,125
Everything that happened

817
01:00:40,150 --> 01:00:41,929
wasn't your fault.

818
01:00:41,954 --> 01:00:46,130
Don't let your whole life
stop at that 18th hole, Vee.

819
01:00:46,155 --> 01:00:48,738
You want me to compete

820
01:00:48,763 --> 01:00:51,196
because you want our course
to become famous again, right?

821
01:00:51,832 --> 01:00:55,257
You want everything to go
perfectly, just like you planned.

822
01:00:56,865 --> 01:01:01,303
But my golfing career
was never that beautiful.

823
01:01:02,222 --> 01:01:05,509
Everything fell apart the day
I chose the trophy

824
01:01:05,534 --> 01:01:07,176
instead of my father.

825
01:01:15,284 --> 01:01:18,213
And now you're asking me
to choose again.

826
01:01:19,573 --> 01:01:21,818
Between my pain

827
01:01:22,590 --> 01:01:24,298
and your success.

828
01:01:26,332 --> 01:01:27,898
And you should know

829
01:01:27,923 --> 01:01:29,174
what I'll choose.

830
01:01:34,922 --> 01:01:37,185
I'm not afraid to compete again.

831
01:01:38,973 --> 01:01:40,108
But I'm afraid that...

832
01:01:40,967 --> 01:01:46,089
this time, you'll be the one
I have to lose.

833
01:01:46,220 --> 01:01:50,713
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

834
01:01:51,361 --> 01:01:56,427
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

835
01:01:56,452 --> 01:02:01,081
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

836
01:02:01,598 --> 01:02:06,347
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

837
01:02:07,009 --> 01:02:08,072
Pro Vee.

838
01:02:09,511 --> 01:02:12,218
Can I be honest with you
about something?

839
01:02:12,385 --> 01:02:17,144
Nana never really
had serious feelings for you.

840
01:02:17,169 --> 01:02:19,640
Dad, is there something
you need to tell us?

841
01:02:19,665 --> 01:02:23,470
Oh, is it about the land
I bought in Khao Yai? Or is it...

842
01:02:23,495 --> 01:02:24,970
About the cancer...

843
01:02:26,542 --> 01:02:28,652
Can I ask you something, Nana?

844
01:02:28,677 --> 01:02:29,834
What is it?

845
01:02:30,471 --> 01:02:32,433
Fahsai told me

846
01:02:32,458 --> 01:02:36,157
that the reason you've been
so nice to me was to use me.

847
01:02:37,864 --> 01:02:42,385
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

848
01:02:42,907 --> 01:02:47,972
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

849
01:02:47,997 --> 01:02:53,188
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

850
01:02:53,213 --> 01:02:58,275
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

851
01:02:58,300 --> 01:03:03,419
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

852
01:03:03,444 --> 01:03:08,402
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

853
01:03:08,427 --> 01:03:11,604
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

854
01:03:11,629 --> 01:03:14,138
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

855
01:03:14,163 --> 01:03:19,711
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

856
01:03:19,737 --> 01:03:22,816
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

857
01:03:22,841 --> 01:03:27,691
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

858
01:03:28,932 --> 01:03:32,079
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

859
01:03:32,104 --> 01:03:34,718
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

860
01:03:34,742 --> 01:03:40,378
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

861
01:03:40,403 --> 01:03:43,606
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

862
01:03:43,631 --> 01:03:45,981
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

863
01:03:46,006 --> 01:03:49,716
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

864
01:03:51,748 --> 01:03:57,102
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

865
01:03:57,127 --> 01:04:02,141
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

866
01:04:02,166 --> 01:04:06,279
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪
